i-arch `.devcontainer/` image (linux/amd64 + arm64) includes bazelisk, buildifier, shfmt, ruff, mypy, ansible, kubectl, helm, kubeconform, shellcheck, bats, yamllint, Node.js 22, Python 3.11, Playwright, and a pinned Grok Build CLI. Versions and checksums are pinned in `.devcontainer/tool-versions.env` (shared with CI). Independent fetch stages keep rebuilds local to the pin that changed. Works on Apple Silicon, Windows (Docker Desktop + WSL2), Linux, and DGX Spark. See dev-environment.md."],[1719,"The Next.js control plane includes an **Observability** section (`#observability`):"],[705,"The NVIDIA GPU Operator works well on K3s but:"],[2893,"The old 64Gi policy floor reserved \\~192 GiB across three Sparks before any Job, so Mode A (\\~189 GiB) always failed and operators clicked through. That made the guard a paper tiger."],[4412,"The orchestrator name (not \"spark0\") is what the generated inventory and `group_vars`\nuse for `k3s_control_plane`. Inventory: generated from `ansible/inventory/lab.yaml`\n(legacy hand-made example: `ansible/inventory/hosts.ini.example`)."],[49,"The output is at `docs/generated/shell/reference.md` and appears in the site under **Reference > Code-Generated Reference**."],[778,"The playbook installs prereqs, highspeed netplan on 2+ nodes (from the generated per-node\nnetplan when present), K3s server on the **orchestrator** node (`role: orchestrator` in\n`lab.yaml`), agents, labels, kubeconfig."],[93,"The previous short paragraph has been replaced by this more complete description."],[1273,"The proxy must stay up if backends are down (per-model 503 is fine)."],[221,"The Shell Commands & Helpers page is **not** written by hand. It is produced from structured comments inside the scripts."],[3385,"The switch block (host, read-only user, `port_map`) lives in `lab.yaml`; the password is\n`LAB_SWITCH_PASSWORD` in the operator's environment only. Qwen 3.5 397B NVFP4 is the\ncanonical TP=4 Job here. Cabling and port map: Choose topology."],[337